{
    "_readme": [
        "Which game art ids each source PNG in design/source-assets/ turns into. Edit this file, not the code.",
        "Keys are PNG file names; the stage folder does not matter. PNGs not listed here are reported and ignored.",
        "type 'islands': a transparent sheet cut into separate figures. 'ids' lists them in reading order:",
        "  rows top to bottom (figures overlapping vertically form a row), left to right within a row.",
        "  Each entry is an id, a list of ids (the first names the file, the rest are aliases of the same image),",
        "  null (drop that figure), or { \"id\": ..., \"also\": [...], \"class\": ... }.",
        "  If the number of figures found differs from the list, the sheet is skipped with a warning.",
        "  Optional: minArea (figure size in half-scale pixels below which a blob counts as a sparkle; default 400),",
        "  threshold (alpha 0-255 that counts as solid when finding figures; default 170).",
        "type 'walk': rows of 6 walk frames; 'rows' lists one id per row, top to bottom. Frames are re-packed",
        "  into equal cells on a shared ground line. If a row does not split into 6 figures, equal-width cells are used.",
        "type 'single': one transparent image, trimmed. type 'scene': an opaque background (not sliced) plus a -small copy.",
        "type 'skip': known file that is not game art.",
        "class (optional, per sheet or per figure) picks the size cap: sprite (620 tall), bust (240 tall), item (160 box),",
        "  icon (160 box), card (500 tall), prop (600 box), panel (1000 box), fx (800 box), logo (1200 wide), scene (1600 wide).",
        "  Without it the class is guessed from the id (see tools/assets/classes.mjs)."
    ],
